abstract: "For 1<alpha<2 and 0<beta<=alpha, log[Gamma(beta)E_{alpha,beta}] is a Bernstein function, so 1/E_{alpha,beta} is completely monotone on the whole triangle below the band [alpha-1,alpha] proposed in Conjecture 25 of Garrappa, Gerhold, Popolizio and Simon (2025). Near alpha=2 the admissible set is exactly (0,b(alpha)] with b analytic, b(2)=3, b'(2)=1+2pi Si(2pi)/(2 I(2pi))=2.82768..., so the band also fails above. Numerical boundary curve and replacement conjecture; exact certificate of a modulus-inequality failure. Unrefereed candidate; internal AI-assisted review only. Text CC0-1.0; code MIT."
